    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95212" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοτό-εις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span>, poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκότιος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dark</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					555
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζόφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.1105
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					188
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοτόεσσα θεῶν πέρι
			δόξα</span> a <i>dark, doubtful</i> opinion, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				132
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκοτοῦσσα</span></b> , ἡ, a town in Thessaly, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(2).11.4
			</span></i> (Tegea, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), etc.; in codd. written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκοτοῦσα</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				10.42.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.5.20
			</span></i>; un
				contr.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκοτόεσσα</span></b> , Poet. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				7.27.6
			</span></i>: Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκοτουσσαῖος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(2).519
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				 iii 9
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Larissa</span>), al.</div>
